From: Orange Pi Zero 3W Linux 6.18 integration
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi-bsp: remove removed MMC_CAP2_HC_ERASE_SZ ABI flag

Linux 6.18 uses BIT(9) in mmc_host::caps2 for MMC_CAP2_SD_UHS2.
The imported Allwinner 6.6 BSP redefines BIT(9) as the removed
MMC_CAP2_HC_ERASE_SZ flag. The active sdmmc@4022000 device-tree node
has the legacy mmc-high-capacity-erase-size property, so its parse
advertises UHS-II although sunxi_mmc_ops has no uhs2_control callback.

Card erase geometry must be derived from MMC core/card initialization,
not an alias of an unrelated capability bit. Stop setting the obsolete
flag and remove its conflicting definition.

Do not change the DTB, real UHS-I capability flags, regulator
sequences, pinctrl, other caps, U-Boot or initramfs in this patch.
Hardware validation and an audit of remaining legacy vendor CAP2 flags
are required before claiming a stable boot.

diff --git a/bsp/drivers/mmc/sunxi-mmc.c b/bsp/drivers/mmc/sunxi-mmc.c
--- a/bsp/drivers/mmc/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/mmc/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -4108,7 +4108,5 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_extra_of_parse(struct mmc_host *mmc)
 
 	np = mmc->parent->of_node;
 
-	if (of_property_read_bool(np, "mmc-high-capacity-erase-size"))
-		mmc->caps2 |= MMC_CAP2_HC_ERASE_SZ;
 	if (sunxi_mmc_chk_hr1b_cap(host)
 			&& of_property_read_bool(np, "cap-wait-while-busy")) {
diff --git a/bsp/drivers/mmc/sunxi-mmc.h b/bsp/drivers/mmc/sunxi-mmc.h
--- a/bsp/drivers/mmc/sunxi-mmc.h
+++ b/bsp/drivers/mmc/sunxi-mmc.h
@@ -643,6 +643,5 @@ struct mmc_gpio {
 #define MMC_CAP2_PACKED_WR	(1 << 13)	/* Allow packed write */
 #define MMC_CAP2_PACKED_CMD	(MMC_CAP2_PACKED_RD | \
 						 MMC_CAP2_PACKED_WR)
-#define MMC_CAP2_HC_ERASE_SZ	(1 << 9)	/* High-capacity erase size */
 
 void sunxi_mmc_select_timing(struct mmc_host *mmc, int64_t value);
